IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `aia-scope`
IMPORT `P3-section-3`

-- P3-art-17: Article 17 of the EU Artificial Intelligence Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744): quality management system.
-- Lines 391-411 of the consolidated text. Paragraph 2 was replaced by the Omnibus (line 408, `▼M1 REPLACED`); paragraphs 1, 3 and 4 are as enacted.
-- Layer 1, the law objectively. The party is "Providers of high-risk AI systems": the role is assumed (Art 3(3), or deemed under Art 25).
-- Reading a result: JUST TRUE the provision is met (or the deeming operates); JUST FALSE the provision applies and is not met, or says no in its own words;
-- NOTHING not covered (the group does not yet apply to this system, Art 2(13) may limit Article 17, or the provision limits itself in its own words).
-- Article 2(13) names Article 17 among the obligations whose application may be limited for an Article 6(1) system: that answer is the gate's (P3-section-3).
-- Seams: S1 (the route, in the `AI system` record), S14, S15 (the gate); Articles 9, 40, 72 and 73 are plain BOOLEAN inputs named for the Article they come from. S12 (SME and SMC) is not taken: the SME wording the Omnibus adds to paragraph 2 is read as emphasis (fork F-17-2).

§ `Article 17(1): the quality management system and the aspects it shall include (a) to (m)`

-- src:394 | (a) a strategy for regulatory compliance, including compliance with conformity assessment procedures and procedures for the management of modifications to the high-risk AI system;
-- src:395 | (b) techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the design, design control and design verification of the high-risk AI system;
-- src:396 | (c) techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the development, quality control and quality assurance of the high-risk AI system;
-- src:397 | (d) examination, test and validation procedures to be carried out before, during and after the development of the high-risk AI system, and the frequency with which they have to be carried out;
-- src:398 | (e) technical specifications, including standards, to be applied and, where the relevant harmonised standards are not applied in full or do not cover all of the relevant requirements set out in Section 2, the means to be used to ensure that the high-risk AI system complies with those requirements;
-- src:399 | (f) systems and procedures for data management, including data acquisition, data collection, data analysis, data labelling, data storage, data filtration, data mining, data aggregation, data retention and any other operation regarding the data that is performed before and for the purpose of the placing on the market or the putting into service of high-risk AI systems;
-- src:400 | (g) the risk management system referred to in Article 9;
-- src:401 | (h) the setting-up, implementation and maintenance of a post-market monitoring system, in accordance with Article 72;
-- src:402 | (i) procedures related to the reporting of a serious incident in accordance with Article 73;
-- src:403 | (j) the handling of communication with national competent authorities, other relevant authorities, including those providing or supporting the access to data, notified bodies, other operators, customers or other interested parties;
-- src:404 | (k) systems and procedures for record-keeping of all relevant documentation and information;
-- src:405 | (l) resource management, including security-of-supply related measures;
-- src:406 | (m) an accountability framework setting out the responsibilities of the management and other staff with regard to all the aspects listed in this paragraph.
@ref Art 17(1)(a) to (m) (src:394-406)
DECLARE `Art 17(1) what the quality management system includes` HAS
    `a strategy for regulatory compliance`                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- (a) including compliance with conformity assessment procedures and procedures for the management of modifications to the high-risk AI system
    `techniques for design, design control and design verification`  IS A BOOLEAN  -- (b) techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the design, design control and design verification
    `techniques for development, quality control and quality assurance` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (c) techniques, procedures and systematic actions to be used for the development, quality control and quality assurance
    `examination, test and validation procedures and their frequency`   IS A BOOLEAN  -- (d) before, during and after the development of the high-risk AI system, and the frequency with which they have to be carried out
    `technical specifications, including standards, and the means to ensure compliance` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (e) where the relevant harmonised standards are not applied in full or do not cover all of the relevant requirements set out in Section 2, the means to be used
    `systems and procedures for data management`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- (f) data acquisition, collection, analysis, labelling, storage, filtration, mining, aggregation, retention and any other operation regarding the data before and for the purpose of placing on the market or putting into service
    `the risk management system referred to in Article 9`     IS A BOOLEAN  -- (g)
    `the post-market monitoring system in accordance with Article 72` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (h) the setting-up, implementation and maintenance
    `procedures related to the reporting of a serious incident in accordance with Article 73` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (i)
    `the handling of communication with authorities, notified bodies, other operators, customers or other interested parties` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (j)
    `systems and procedures for record-keeping of all relevant documentation and information` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (k)
    `resource management, including security-of-supply related measures` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (l)
    `an accountability framework for the responsibilities of the management and other staff` IS A BOOLEAN  -- (m) with regard to all the aspects listed in this paragraph

-- "shall include at least the following aspects": every one of the thirteen is needed; more may be included.
