@ref Art 17(1) (a) to (m) (src:394-406)
GIVEN `the aspects` IS AN `Art 17(1) what the quality management system includes`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1) the quality management system includes at least the aspects listed in points (a) to (m)` MEANS
        `the aspects`'s `a strategy for regulatory compliance`
    AND `the aspects`'s `techniques for design, design control and design verification`
    AND `the aspects`'s `techniques for development, quality control and quality assurance`
    AND `the aspects`'s `examination, test and validation procedures and their frequency`
    AND `the aspects`'s `technical specifications, including standards, and the means to ensure compliance`
    AND `the aspects`'s `systems and procedures for data management`
    AND `the aspects`'s `the risk management system referred to in Article 9`
    AND `the aspects`'s `the post-market monitoring system in accordance with Article 72`
    AND `the aspects`'s `procedures related to the reporting of a serious incident in accordance with Article 73`
    AND `the aspects`'s `the handling of communication with authorities, notified bodies, other operators, customers or other interested parties`
    AND `the aspects`'s `systems and procedures for record-keeping of all relevant documentation and information`
    AND `the aspects`'s `resource management, including security-of-supply related measures`
    AND `the aspects`'s `an accountability framework for the responsibilities of the management and other staff`

-- src:393 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems shall put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation. That system shall be documented in a systematic and orderly manner in the form of written policies, procedures and instructions, and shall include at least the following aspects:
@ref Art 17(1) (src:393)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the quality management system ensures compliance with this Regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the quality management system is documented in a systematic and orderly manner in the form of written policies, procedures and instructions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the aspects` IS AN `Art 17(1) what the quality management system includes`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(1) the provider has put in place a quality management system that meets paragraph 1` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF       `the quality management system ensures compliance with this Regulation`
             AND `the quality management system is documented in a systematic and orderly manner in the form of written policies, procedures and instructions`
             AND `Art 17(1) the quality management system includes at least the aspects listed in points (a) to (m)` `the aspects`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Providers of high-risk AI systems shall put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation. That system shall be documented in a systematic and orderly manner ... and shall include at least the following aspects"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)

§ `Article 17(2): proportionality (replaced by the Omnibus: as enacted and as amended)`

DECLARE `Art 17 act` IS ONE OF
    `Art 17(1) put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation`
    `Art 17(2) implement the aspects referred to in paragraph 1 proportionately to the size of the provider's organisation`
    `Art 17(2) respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required to ensure the compliance of the high-risk AI systems with this Regulation`
    `Art 17(3) include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to sectoral Union law`

-- VERSION as enacted. No date and no gate: the dispatcher below never reaches it (Chapter III Sections 1 to 3 apply only after 27 July 2026), so the text as enacted is tested through this function.
