§ `Article 17(3): sectoral quality management systems (a permission: "may include")`

-- "Providers ... that are subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law may include the aspects ...".
-- A function named for a power answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE, when its gate fails (ruling of 2026-11-12, limit 1); fork F-17-3 in NOTES.md.
-- src:410 | 3. Providers of high-risk AI systems that are subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law may include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to that law.
@ref Art 17(3) (src:410)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(3) the provider may include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to sectoral Union law` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the provider is subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Providers of high-risk AI systems that are subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law may include the aspects"; a grant named "may" (ruling of 2026-11-12)
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)

§ `Article 17(4): financial institutions (the obligation is "deemed to be fulfilled")`

-- The deeming covers "the obligation to put in place a quality management system, with the exception of paragraph 1, points (g), (h) and (i)". An aspect is named by its letter in paragraph 1 ("a" to "m").
-- JUST FALSE for the three aspects the text excepts (its own words); JUST TRUE for another aspect where the provider is such a financial institution and complies with the rules on internal governance;
-- NOTHING where the deeming does not operate on the facts (the text says the obligation is deemed fulfilled "by complying", and nothing else about a provider that does not) or the letter is not an aspect of paragraph 1.
-- src:411 | 4. For providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law, the obligation to put in place a quality management system, with the exception of paragraph 1, points (g), (h) and (i) of this Article, shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes pursuant to the relevant Union financial services law. To that end, any harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 shall be taken into account.
@ref Art 17(4) (src:411)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the aspect of paragraph 1, by its letter` IS A STRING
      `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider complies with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes pursuant to the relevant Union financial services law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(4) the obligation to put in place a quality management system is deemed to be fulfilled as to the aspect` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF NOT (elem `the aspect of paragraph 1, by its letter` (LIST "a", "b", "c", "d", "e", "f", "g", "h", "i", "j", "k", "l", "m"))
        THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraph 1 has aspects (a) to (m) only
        ELSE IF elem `the aspect of paragraph 1, by its letter` (LIST "g", "h", "i")
             THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "with the exception of paragraph 1, points (g), (h) and (i) of this Article"
             ELSE IF       `the provider is a financial institution subject to requirements regarding its internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law`
                       AND `the provider complies with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes pursuant to the relevant Union financial services law`
                  THEN JUST TRUE
                  ELSE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes"; the text says nothing of a provider that is not such an institution or does not comply
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)

-- "To that end, any harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 shall be taken into account." No actor is named, so there is no regulative rule; the decision function asks whether they were.
-- src:411 | 4. For providers that are financial institutions subject to requirements regarding their internal governance, arrangements or processes under Union financial services law, the obligation to put in place a quality management system, with the exception of paragraph 1, points (g), (h) and (i) of this Article, shall be deemed to be fulfilled by complying with the rules on internal governance arrangements or processes pursuant to the relevant Union financial services law. To that end, any harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 shall be taken into account.
@ref Art 17(4) second sentence (src:411)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 have been taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Art 17(4) the harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 have been taken into account` MEANS
    CONSIDER gate
    WHEN `Section 3 applies` THEN
        IF `the harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 have been taken into account`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "To that end, any harmonised standards referred to in Article 40 shall be taken into account"
    OTHERWISE `Section 3 the answer when the gate is shut` gate
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)

§ `Regulative rules of Article 17 (each is a MUST or MAY with no time limit; no trace can show a breach)`

-- src:393 | 1. Providers of high-risk AI systems shall put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation. That system shall be documented in a systematic and orderly manner in the form of written policies, procedures and instructions, and shall include at least the following aspects:
@ref Art 17(1) (src:393)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 17 act`
`Art 17(1) the provider's duty to put a quality management system in place` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 17(1) put a quality management system in place that ensures compliance with this Regulation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "no quality management system that ensures compliance with this Regulation was put in place"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)


-- src:408 | 2. The implementation of the aspects referred to in paragraph 1 shall be proportionate to the size of the provider’s organisation, in particular, if the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC. Providers shall, in any event, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required to ensure the compliance of their high-risk AI systems with this Regulation.
@ref Art 17(2) (src:408)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 17 act`
`Art 17(2) the provider's duty to implement the aspects proportionately to the size of its organisation` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 17(2) implement the aspects referred to in paragraph 1 proportionately to the size of the provider's organisation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the aspects were not implemented proportionately to the size of the provider's organisation"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)


-- src:408 | 2. The implementation of the aspects referred to in paragraph 1 shall be proportionate to the size of the provider’s organisation, in particular, if the provider is an SME, including a start-up, or an SMC. Providers shall, in any event, respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required to ensure the compliance of their high-risk AI systems with this Regulation.
@ref Art 17(2) second sentence (src:408)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 17 act`
`Art 17(2) the provider's duty to respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MUST `Art 17(2) respect the degree of rigour and the level of protection required to ensure the compliance of the high-risk AI systems with this Regulation`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY Provider BECAUSE "the degree of rigour and the level of protection required were not respected"
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is owed: the gate is shut or Art 2(2) cuts the Article off
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)


-- Article 17(3): a permission. A MAY with no consequence cannot be breached (and `MAY ... LEST` degrades on main, so none is written).
-- src:410 | 3. Providers of high-risk AI systems that are subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law may include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to that law.
@ref Art 17(3) (src:410)
GIVEN `the date asked` IS A DATE
      `the AI system` IS AN `AI system`
      `the circumstances` IS A `Section 3 circumstances`
      `the provider is subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Role `Art 17 act`
`Art 17(3) the provider's permission to include the aspects as part of the quality management systems pursuant to sectoral Union law` MEANS
    IF `Section 3 the gate is open` gate AND `the provider is subject to obligations regarding quality management systems or an equivalent function under relevant sectoral Union law`
    THEN PARTY Provider
         MAY `Art 17(3) include the aspects listed in paragraph 1 as part of the quality management systems pursuant to sectoral Union law`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED  -- nothing is permitted or owed: the gate is shut, Art 2(2) cuts the Article off, or the provider is not subject to such obligations
    WHERE
        gate MEANS `Section 3 gate` `the date asked` `the AI system` `the circumstances` (`Article reference` OF 17, "", 0)
